From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:41:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] DPP: Accept the Multi-AP backhaul netRoles in Network Introduction

A Multi-AP Controller signs a Connector with netRole "mapBackhaulSta"
for a backhaul STA and one with netRole "mapBackhaulBss" for a backhaul
BSS. Wi-Fi EasyMesh v6.1, 5.3.3, Table 8 makes the two compatible in the
Connector group comparison (Easy Connect 3.0, 6.6.5) and recommends a
case insensitive match. dpp_compatible_netrole() accepts only "sta" with
"ap", so Network Introduction between a backhaul STA and a backhaul BSS
ends with STATUS_NO_MATCH, and the backhaul cannot use the DPP AKM.

Accept the backhaul pair as well. The other pairs of Table 8 (mapAgent
with mapAgent or mapController) apply to the 1905 layer, and hostapd and
wpa_supplicant run Network Introduction only over Wi-Fi.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/common/dpp.c
+++ b/src/common/dpp.c
@@ -4104,10 +4104,20 @@ fail:
 }
 
 
+static int dpp_compatible_map_netrole(const char *role1, const char *role2)
+{
+	return (os_strcasecmp(role1, "mapBackhaulSta") == 0 &&
+		os_strcasecmp(role2, "mapBackhaulBss") == 0) ||
+		(os_strcasecmp(role1, "mapBackhaulBss") == 0 &&
+		 os_strcasecmp(role2, "mapBackhaulSta") == 0);
+}
+
+
 static int dpp_compatible_netrole(const char *role1, const char *role2)
 {
 	return (os_strcmp(role1, "sta") == 0 && os_strcmp(role2, "ap") == 0) ||
-		(os_strcmp(role1, "ap") == 0 && os_strcmp(role2, "sta") == 0);
+		(os_strcmp(role1, "ap") == 0 && os_strcmp(role2, "sta") == 0) ||
+		dpp_compatible_map_netrole(role1, role2);
 }
 
 
